### Competitor & Factual Verification

- **Competitor URL:** Blank in source row (no synthetic competitor URL invented).
- **Factual & Legal Due Diligence:**
  - **BIS Hallmarking Exemption:** Under official Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) regulations, jewellery items weighing **under 2 grams** are exempt from mandatory laser hallmarking to prevent structural damage to ultra-thin shanks. Reputable fine jewellers (like BlueStone) issue comprehensive itemized tax invoices and authenticity certificates specifying net gold weight, karatage (14K/18K), and lifetime buyback/exchange rights.
  - **Material Truth & Alloy Hardness:** Addressed the crucial difference between genuine solid gold (14K/18K) versus "1-gram micro gold-plated / forming gold" brass imitation rings. Explained why 14K and 18K solid gold alloys provide superior tensile strength and bend-resistance compared to soft 22K gold for ultra-lightweight rings.
  - **Citations:** [Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS)](https://www.bis.gov.in/).

